%0 Conference Paper
%T Analysing Chain of Thought Dynamics: Active Guidance or Unfaithful Post-hoc Rationalisation?
%A Samuel Lewis-Lim
%A Xingwei Tan
%A Zhixue Zhao
%A Nikolaos Aletras
%D 2025
%J Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing
%X Recent work has demonstrated that Chain-of-Thought (CoT) often yields limited gains for soft-reasoning problems such as analytical and commonsense reasoning. CoT can also be unfaithful to a model's actual reasoning. We investigate the dynamics and faithfulness of CoT in soft-reasoning tasks across instruction-tuned, reasoning and reasoning-distilled models. Our findings reveal differences in how these models rely on CoT, and show that CoT influence and faithfulness are not always aligned.
